{
  "sn12.28:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.28 ",
  "sn12.28:0.2": "3. The Ten Powers ",
  "sn12.28:0.3": "A Mendicant ",
  "sn12.28:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.28:1.2": "",
  "sn12.28:1.3": "“A mendicant understands old age and death, their origin, their cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation. They understand rebirth … ",
  "sn12.28:1.4": "continued existence … ",
  "sn12.28:1.5": "grasping … ",
  "sn12.28:1.6": "craving … ",
  "sn12.28:1.7": "feeling … ",
  "sn12.28:1.8": "contact … ",
  "sn12.28:1.9": "the six sense fields … ",
  "sn12.28:1.10": "name and form … ",
  "sn12.28:1.11": "consciousness … ",
  "sn12.28:1.12": "They understand choices, their origin, their cessation, and the practice that leads to their cessation. ",
  "sn12.28:2.1": "And what is old age and death? ",
  "sn12.28:2.2": "The old age, decrepitude, broken teeth, grey hair, wrinkly skin, diminished vitality, and failing faculties of the various sentient beings in the various orders of sentient beings. ",
  "sn12.28:2.3": "This is called old age. ",
  "sn12.28:2.4": "The passing away, passing on, disintegration, demise, mortality, death, decease, breaking up of the aggregates, and laying to rest of the corpse of the various sentient beings in the various orders of sentient beings. ",
  "sn12.28:2.5": "This is called death. ",
  "sn12.28:2.6": "Such is old age, and such is death. ",
  "sn12.28:2.7": "This is called old age and death. ",
  "sn12.28:2.8": "Rebirth is the origin of old age and death. "